{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>With fire she shall be burned.</b> If it had said תשרף באש it would appear to mean a burning by fire — that is, with a pile of wood and a fire-pyre. But the law of Torah regarding death by burning is not so, to burn the form of the body with actual fire, Heaven forbid. And so I have found that the Sages, of blessed memory, deduced this from what they expounded in Pesaḥim, chapter Keitzad Tzolin: ״באש תשרף״ — to include all burnings that come about by means of fire, and Rav Matnah said: a thread of [molten] lead [placed] on the organ. For regarding the bulls that are burned it is written ״ושרף אותו על עצים באש״ — ״באש״ yes, by anything else, no; here it is written ״באש תשרף״, to include all burnings that come about by means of fire. And they needed to say so, for the intent of death by burning is like the burning of the sons of Aharon — a burning of the soul while the body remains intact."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:33.610197426Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}